{"id": "EUVD-2026-106997", "enisaUuid": "993db06f-042b-3a18-a7e4-92f01e799f48", "description": "FreeRDP 3.0.0 before 3.32.0 contains a null-pointer dereference in the smartcard emulation backend that accepts a null per-reader name in SCardGetStatusChange requests. A malicious RDP server can send a crafted reader-state entry with a null szReader, causing strcmp or _wcscmp to crash the client process.", "datePublished": "2026-10-21T00:36:24", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T00:36:24", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/FreeRDP/FreeRDP/security/advisories/GHSA-q6pp-28g8-xqjc", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/freerdp-3.0.0-before-3.32.0-null-pointer-dereference-via-emulated-smartcard"], "aliases": ["GHSA-546m-xj3q-7gh4", "CVE-2026-114046"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.25, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "e18bf34b-b4c1-37b4-adff-a9c91d6cbc09", "product": {"name": "FreeRDP", "vendor": {"name": "FreeRDP"}}, "product_version": "3.0.0 <3.32.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "793073cd-e70a-31fa-aeda-429fd0c0499a", "vendor": {"name": "FreeRDP"}}], "isExploited": false}